WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.120
Paul Feig, the Director who has made "The Heat"

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.200
and "Bridesmaids" and "Spy",

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.930
and the best things ever in life,

4
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.690
he is delivering none other than "Welcome to Flatch"

5
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.070
which is your news series.

6
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.100
Tell us about it.

7
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.260
It's a docu-comedy in the vein

8
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.260 line:15%
of "Modern Family", "The office", "Parks and Rec".

9
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.740 line:15%
And what is really exciting about it,

10
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.040
it's based on a British show called "This country",

11
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.420
but it's also filled with people you haven't seen before.

12
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.320
And I think it's really nice to watch a show

13
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.420
where you get to discover a bunch of new, amazing comedians

14
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.750
'cause we sort of see the same faces over and over again.

15
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.500
And this is like new talent and the next generation

16
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.250
of brilliant people who you're gonna watch

17
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.083
for years to come.

18
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:46.270
I also just trust Paul Feig so much.

19
00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.520
He's made some of the great comedies

20
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.250
and he knows how to balance heart and humor.

21
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.990
And to me, when you have the potent combination

22
00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.640
of those two things, it's everything.

23
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.261
Yeah, we all need a laugh right now.

24
00:01:00.261 --> 00:01:03.995
(audience applaud)

25
00:01:03.995 --> 00:01:05.520
Is it true that you stole something

26
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.843
from "Welcome to Flatch?"?

27
00:01:07.843 --> 00:01:10.163
Well, I wouldn't call it stealing.

28
00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.283
So I eat a lot of PB and J.

29
00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.960
You mean something a little like this?

30
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.090
Yes.
(audience applaud)

31
00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.490
I often get them as snacks on set.

32
00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.860
And so one day the director of photography was walking by

33
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.327
and she had a PB and J in her hand and I went,

34
00:01:29.327 --> 00:01:30.580
"Oh, that's for me."

35
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:33.640
Because they tend to give me PB and Js

36
00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:34.760
to keep my blood sugar up.

37
00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.470
And I grabbed it out of her hand and took it

38
00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.500
and ate it and then looked around and realized

39
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.720
that suddenly everyone had PB and Js and that I had just-

40
00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.290
You didn't need to steal hers?

41
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.670
No, that was her PB and J

42
00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.020
that I took right out of her hand.

43
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.540
And what I realized was because she didn't say anything,

44
00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.610
I must be scary enough that she thought I was that person

45
00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.973
that would just take something out of her hand.

46
00:01:57.835 --> 00:01:59.780
It was an odd occurrence.

47
00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.710
So will you play a little game with me?

48
00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:02.543
Yeah.

49
00:02:02.543 --> 00:02:05.924
All right, it's Q&amp;A with PB and J.

50
00:02:05.924 --> 00:02:08.280
(audience cheer and applaud)

51
00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.460
All right, I'm gonna eat one too.

52
00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.693
All right, take a big bite.

53
00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.630 line:15%
Which celebrity would be your hall pass and why?

54
00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:20.723 line:15%
Oh, well, I wish I had gone

55
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.825 line:15%
for George Costanza from "Seinfeld."

56
00:02:25.825 --> 00:02:29.090
(audience cheer and applaud)

57
00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:32.510
You know, George's quest to have sex and eat a sandwich

58
00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.690
at the same time is like my favorite episode.

59
00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:36.523
Call me.

60
00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.950
We're pulling a Costanza right now.

61
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:43.350
All right, a TV show that you recommend for us to binge.

62
00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.329
What are you watching?

63
00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:45.162
What are you into?

64
00:02:45.162 --> 00:02:48.130
"Love Island UK".
(audience cheer and applaud)

65
00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.830
What's your favorite ID account?

66
00:02:51.209 --> 00:02:52.540
I really love The Dodo.

67
00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.990
I love The Dodo.

68
00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:56.130
Yeah, if I'm on Instagram,

69
00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.930
it's 'cause I'm watching dog videos.

70
00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.864
Have you ever woken up somewhere

71
00:03:00.864 --> 00:03:03.120
and you didn't know what happened?

72
00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.690
I have something called vasovagal syncope.

73
00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.670
What is that?

74
00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:09.223
That makes me black out.

75
00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.930
Like without drinking?

76
00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:15.670
Without drinking, if I hit my elbow in a certain way,

77
00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.530
like I've fallen off a chair.

78
00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.803
So I was on a stilt walk.

79
00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.970
We were stilt walking through the forest

80
00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.160
and I fell off the stilt.

81
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.500
So I woke up in the middle of the forest with stilts

82
00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.040
on my feet.

83
00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.069
I was not expecting this answer at all.

84
00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:31.510
I know, a little less naughty.

85
00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.050
I mean I blacked out, but I did it to myself,

86
00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.480
if you know what I mean.

87
00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:39.513
Well, I have to tell you Aya Cash,

88
00:03:39.513 --> 00:03:42.650
I've had so much fun with you today

89
00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.730
and I totally celebrate you,

90
00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.223
and I'm so glad that you came here today, thank you.

91
00:03:48.223 --> 00:03:50.084
Well, thank you.
(audience applaud)

92
00:03:50.084 --> 00:03:52.292
And thank you for lunch.

93
00:03:52.292 --> 00:03:54.080
Okay, I have to add, "The girl from Plainville"

94
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.890
is now streaming on Hulu

95
00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.820
and "Welcome to Flatch" airs Thursday

96
00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.550
at 9:30 Eastern on Fox.

97
00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:01.730
They're both incredible.

98
00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:03.563
Thank you for everything you're putting out into the world.

99
00:04:03.563 --> 00:04:06.146 line:15%
(upbeat music)

